{"id":"3765fb2168038a13","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski.md","title":"Ehrenfeucht-Mostowski Theorem","display":"thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski — Ehrenfeucht-Mostowski Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski","aliases":["17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski"],"display":"thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski — Ehrenfeucht-Mostowski Theorem","depends_on":["[[17-df-linear-order]]","[[17-df-indiscernible-sequence]]","[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_verification":"statement and compactness proof compared in supplied OCR; local injective-sequence formulation","source_section":"3.3","source_result":"Theorem 3.3.10; Lemma 3.3.9","source_pages_print":[170,171],"source_pages_djvu":[186,187],"legacy_label":"17-thm-2.4.2","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski — Ehrenfeucht-Mostowski Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9c54640eb3282127\" href=\"?note=9c54640eb3282127\" title=\"17-df-indiscernible-sequence\">17-df-indiscernible-sequence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"statement and compactness proof compared in supplied OCR; local injective-sequence formulation"},{"key":"source_section","html":"3.3"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Theorem 3.3.10; Lemma 3.3.9"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>170</span><span>171</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>186</span><span>187</span></div>"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-2.4.2"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-theory)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> is a set and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"{&lt;}\\subseteq I\\times I\">\\({&lt;}\\subseteq I\\times I\\)</span> is a candidate strict order. <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\">\\(\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\\)</span> is the strict linear-order predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> (model class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,&lt;}(\\mathfrak A)\">\\(\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,&lt;}(\\mathfrak A)\\)</span> (order-indiscernible sequences, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"9c54640eb3282127\" href=\"?note=9c54640eb3282127\" title=\"17-df-indiscernible-sequence\">17-df-indiscernible-sequence</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\">\\(\\aleph_0\\)</span> (least infinite cardinal, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\n\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\exists a\\in\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,&lt;}(\\mathfrak A)\\;\n\\forall i,j\\in I\\;\n\\bigl(a(i)=a(j)\\to i=j\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\n\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\exists a\\in\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,&lt;}(\\mathfrak A)\\;\n\\forall i,j\\in I\\;\n\\bigl(a(i)=a(j)\\to i=j\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The injectivity clause makes the indiscernible sequence indexed by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> into an ordered subset of the model.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This is Theorem 3.3.10, printed p.171 (DjVu187). Its proof adds distinct constants indexed by the ordered set and the indiscernibility equivalences. Every finite collection embeds into the natural-number order, so Lemma 3.3.9 (printed p.170, DjVu186), proved by Ramsey thinning, gives finite satisfiability. Compactness then gives the required model. The local catalog label differs from the book result number.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-linear-order","status":"resolved","id":"3f12d30db6793ecd","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-linear-order]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-indiscernible-sequence","status":"resolved","id":"9c54640eb3282127","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-indiscernible-sequence]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic","status":"resolved","id":"0c4dd6e6f689f962","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-linear-order","status":"resolved","id":"3f12d30db6793ecd","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$I$ is a set and ${<}\\subseteq I\\times I$ is a candidate strict order. $\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,<)$ is the strict linear-order predicate from [[17-df-linear-order]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Mod}(T)$ (model class, see [[17-df-model]])","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-indiscernible-sequence","status":"resolved","id":"9c54640eb3282127","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,<}(\\mathfrak A)$ (order-indiscernible sequences, see [[17-df-indiscernible-sequence]])","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic","status":"resolved","id":"0c4dd6e6f689f962","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\aleph_0$ (least infinite cardinal, see [[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}","display":false},{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"I","display":false},{"tex":"{<}\\subseteq I\\times I","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,<)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,<}(\\mathfrak A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\aleph_0","display":false},{"tex":"\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,<)\n\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\exists a\\in\\operatorname{Ind}_{I,<}(\\mathfrak A)\\;\n\\forall i,j\\in I\\;\n\\bigl(a(i)=a(j)\\to i=j\\bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"I","display":false}],"bytes":2253,"backlinks":[{"id":"9c54640eb3282127","anchor":"ref-10","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"原书 §3.3 印刷 p.169（DjVu185）以有序子集定义不可分辨元；本地以任意序列记录该条件，并在 [[17-thm-ehrenfeucht-mostowski]] 中另加单射性以得到有序子集。"},{"id":"2c98c9e634ff4b44","anchor":"ref-173","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-thm-aleph-one-categoricity-consequences]]\n[[17-thm-atomic-model-existence]]\n[[17-thm-beth-definability]]\n[[17-thm-beth-definability-satisfaction-form]]\n[[17-thm-chain-sentence-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-chain-theory-preservation]]\n[[17-thm-compactness]]\n[[17-thm-compactness-equivalents]]\n[[17-thm-compactness-henkin-form]]\n[[17-thm-compa